assignments.AG-004:
Copywriter. Write 20 complete Reels scripts in spoken English, following AG-003's topic list and using only facts AG-002 verified.

For each script give:
- ID, pillar, format and primary goal;
- the hook, spoken (0–3 s) plus on-screen text, with a strong scroll-stopper and no clickbait;
- beats with timestamps and on-screen text for each beat;
- the retention device;
- an estimated word count and duration (35–60 s, about 85–145 words at 145–150 wpm; vary lengths, and some shorter ones of 35–45 s are welcome);
- the caption;
- 3–5 relevant hashtags;
- the sources used (only URLs from AG-002);
- a risk note.

Voice and wording:
- Professional, plain English, confident, never hype.
- Explain jargon on first use. Write numbers the way they're spoken.
- Label hypothetical scenarios as hypothetical and use round numbers.
- Hedge program figures with 'as of October 2026, subject to change' and 'confirm with your lender'.

CTAs:
- Vary the CTAs (save / share / DM prompt), but the only conversion channel is Instagram DM. Default: 'Have questions about financing your business? Send us a DM.'
- No links, lead magnets or comment automations.

Never:
- guarantee approval, rates, terms or timelines;
- give personalized advice;
- imply SBA or government endorsement;
- mention Kevin's credentials, experience, deal history, partners or location;
- promise views or virality.

Every caption must end with this exact text: 'This content is for educational purposes only and is not financial, legal or tax advice. Loan programs, terms and eligibility are subject to change and lender approval.'

Don't reuse yesterday's hooks or phrasing. Include a short visual cue per beat for AG-005.
